# chktex configuration for this conjecture. Run from this directory:
#
#     chktex -q statement.tex
#
# Three warnings are suppressed, checked hit by hit on 28 August 2026
# rather than assumed, each with a 100% false-positive rate in this file:
#
#   3   "You should enclose the previous parenthesis with `{}'." Both hits are
#       $\Unif((\Fq^{n})^{T})$, where the superscript T attaches to the closing
#       parenthesis exactly as intended -- T-tuples of length-n vectors.  (2 hits)
#   8   "Wrong length of dash may have been used." The single hit is the en-dash
#       in "dense--sparse LPN", inside a sentence quoted verbatim from the
#       source, which prints an en-dash there. Changing it would misquote.  (1 hit)
#   38  "You should not use punctuation in front of quotes." Each of the 3 hits
#       is the final character of a sentence quoted verbatim from the source.
#       The punctuation belongs to the quoted text.  (3 hits)
#
# Everything else stays on. As of 28 August 2026 the file is clean under
# this config and `lacheck statement.tex` is silent.

CmdLine
{
    -n3
    -n8
    -n38
}
